Subject: RE: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note


 
Dear Fabio,
 
Please find attached the draft proposal for Corridor 11 - South Sudan with a view to contracting before the end of the year, focusing on improving trade facilitation and transport infrastructure
 to increase cross-border trade. 
 
Please note that we have received this version only today after a previous version yesterday. Some basic issues should now be corrected but it should still be work in progress. We are
 looking forward to comments from you and our colleagues in the Ugandan delegation to improve further.

 
We have decided to work with two implementing partners (UNOPS and ITC). UNOPS will work on the infrastructure components, while ITC will work on the soft components of trade and markets.
 UNOPS has extensive experience in implementing EU-funded infrastructure projects and ITC has experience of working on trade issues in South Sudan.
 
We would be grateful if you could indicate the way forward after this submission to secure this regional funding for South Sudan. Please, let us know if you would like to have a follow
 up meeting to discuss any comments and consolidate a common response for UNOPS/ITC.
 
Kind regards,
 
Sunday
 
 
 


