Subject: Re: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 Intervention Logic


 
Dear Fiona, dear colleagues,
 
Many thanks for the note and the work on developing this logic of intervention
We really appreciated the efforts in putting together i) the ongoing existing work with future proposals  ii) and including and making the link between hard infra and soft measures.

 
We had a discussion in HQ with all the concerned corridor units (A4, E2,F4) to look at all intervention logics. Given the current political context, we understand and agree with your proposal
 of limit the scope of interventions on the Uganda- South Sudan border for the moment.
 
With regards to the trade and transport facilitation measures, we suggest to plan in 2024 an action (indicative envelop 15M)  focusing
on small-scale cross border traders (including also the relevant border post activities mentioned), which links very well with the context and logic of intervention explained. Please go ahead on the project preparation and share with us a concept note
 as soon as ready and indicative contracting period.
 
With regards to the hard measures please go ahead with the preparatory work for hard infra projects and let us know if there are any needs for the feasibility/preparatory works.

Kind regards,  
Fabio and colleagues

 


