Subject: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take aways meeting 6th December


 
Dear colleagues,

 
Many thanks for your active participation on 6/12 in this first subregional coordination meeting. The main objective of the meeting was to ensure a better coordination at subregional level and
 to set up a system that reinforces the way of working in a more coherent way, connecting the different levels of intervention (corridor- regional- continental).
Attached you can find the PPT that was presented. We note that there were some elements missing and to be corrected, we will work on it for the next session.
 
Please see below some takeaways and comments, let us know if there is anything missing that needs to be urgently addressed.

 
Main takeaways:

-         
Important to have this sub-regional vision to share experiences form corridor to corridor and to ensure that budgetary commitments under the Eastern-Central Africa budget lines are respected. Suggest to organize
 this regional coordination meeting on a monthly basis (recurrent invitation to be shared by HQ).


-         
Meetings for coordination at corridor level to continue in parallel, led by lead EUD. Exchanges with HQ per corridor will also continue in parallel to continue finetuning proposals.


-         
Important to define a narrative/ logic of intervention along the corridors that guide the proposed interventions per corridor -
(corridor approach justification).

-         
Lead Delegations role welcomed by participants, lead EUD to ensure the coordination and gathering of input for definition of corridor approach and for the submission of proposals to HQ.


-         
Proposals for action along the corridors can be shaped as standalone individual projects contributing to the defined corridor logic
(ie. Port of Dar er Salam proposal) or shaped under a unified proposal to cover the overall corridor (ie. corridor Douala- Kampala).
Contracting authority can be different from the lead EUD. 

-         
HQ to develop and share (January 2024) a document/file that could allow monitoring all updates and proposals in a more automatic way, as well as to share info on what is being done (access to all EUDs).

-         
Important to look at all support measures in a more integrated manner. HQ to further reflect on a system that allows to see all (soft and hard) proposals in a comprehensive way.

-         
HQ to set up a decision system (with geographic and thematic units) that will allow joint decision making with a broader subregional vision linked to the budget lines. Tentative calendar find below.

-         
To have a more regular system and make sure that contracting is done within N+1, we would suggest to have 2 periods in which proposals can be submitted and reviewed within the broader vision.

 
Corridor by corridor observations:

-         
Corridor 5, lead Delegation is finetuning unified proposal along the corridor. More developed concept note will be shared for comments and feedback. Good to have indicative contracting foreseen.

-         
Corridor 6, lead Delegation has sent already the proposed approach. Overall very clear and we now expect a more developed concept with indicative contracting timeline for comments and feedback

-         
Corridor 7, *
Exceptionally and considering the urgency in terms of timing, feedback and way forward will be shared for the Dar er Salam proposal (corridor 7) before end 2024.
In parallel, lead Delegation with National EUDs to work in the development of the corridor logic (including the port proposal) and assess the relevance of other interventions proposed along the corridor.


-         
Corridor 8, lead Delegation finetuning unified proposal and working in consolidating different country proposals. More developed concept note will be shared for comments and feedback.
*On the “Joint border post proposal” to confirm whether this would fit in the proposal that will be submitted or requires urgent ad-hoc discussion (similar to Dar er Salam), indicate timeline.


-         
Corridor 11, lead Delegation to finetune the proposal and confirm whether this would be the full intervention in the corridor, together with overall corridor logic approach for intervention.
 
Proposed calendar -
focused on budget N+1 2024 – 31.3 M€
 




By 20th January



Lead Delegations to share brief paragraph with the intended approach and narrative guiding the work in the corridor
(logic of intervention and focus of action). 




By 15th March 


Lead EUDs to share mature proposals (concept note/s) to be contracted before the end of the year 2024
(1st round)




By 1st April


HQ (A4, E2, F4, A2) to send feedback and way forward for contracting on the corridor proposals





By 15th May


Lead EUDs to share mature proposals (concept note/s) to be contracted before the end of the year 2024
(2nd round) and if ready also for 2025




By 1st June


HQ (A4, E2, F4, A2) to send feedback and way forward for contracting on the corridor proposals




 
 
Fabio, Macarena, Georgios
 

